## Using the data

Original source files live in `data/original/` and are never edited in place. The tidy outputs in `data/processed/` are regenerated from them by code; `docs/data-dictionary.md` explains every column (type, units, missingness, caveats).

<!-- IF:PIPELINE -->```sh
git clone {{REPO_URL}}
cd {{PROJECT_SLUG}}
uv sync                                   # install (Python >= 3.12)
uv run python -m scripts.pipeline run     # regenerate data/processed/ from the originals
uv run pytest                             # tests
```

For the R variant: `make restore` (renv) then `make pipeline` (targets).
