## License

Code, data and documentation are licensed separately, because the law treats them differently and a single license rarely fits all three. Without an explicit license, reuse defaults to "all rights reserved," which quietly forbids the reuse an open project invites.

| Layer | Covers | License (SPDX) |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Code | `scripts/`, pipelines, notebooks | `{{LICENSE}}` (see `LICENSE`) |
| Data | `data/processed/` and released tables | `<CC-BY-4.0 or CC0-1.0>` |
| Documentation | README, `docs/`, figures | `<CC-BY-4.0>` |

`LICENSE` governs the code. Choose the data license by how much attribution you need: CC BY 4.0 requires credit, CC0 maximizes reuse. Upstream sources can constrain what may be re-released; reconcile the data license with each source's terms (recorded in provenance) before publishing.

